{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8pYBQ31zzGMwpa7pGdo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G9VTS62rJQTmNVLb1ozwat","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/webtorrent-desktop.memory-leaks-12-window-bounds-debounce-one-thread && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src-tauri/AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nanchor='## Gates\\n'\nadd='''## Background work from a window event gets one worker, not a thread each\n\nTauri delivers `WindowEvent`s on the UI thread, and a drag delivers\nhundreds of them. `window::Debounce` is the pattern for work that must\nleave that thread: one worker, started on the first call, sleeping on a\n`Condvar` until a deadline every call pushes forward, and ending when\nthe last clone is dropped. A `std::thread::spawn` per event is what it\nreplaced. Its tests make \"one worker\" observable by recording\n`std::thread::current().id()` from each job across several bursts.\n\n'''\ns=s.replace(anchor, add+anchor,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat >> .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Implemented\n- src-tauri/src/window.rs: `Debounce` now holds an `Arc<Handle>` over a\n  `Mutex<Pending>` + `Condvar`. `call` stores the newest job, moves the\n  deadline to now + delay, and lazily spawns the single worker. The worker\n  waits until the deadline passes unmoved, runs the job outside the lock\n  (wrapped in catch_unwind so a panicking job cannot kill the worker), and\n  exits once every clone is dropped and nothing is pending.\n- Public API unchanged (`new`, `call`, Clone, Debug); main.rs untouched.\n\n## Tests (src-tauri/src/window.rs)\n- every_burst_runs_on_the_one_worker: red on the old code (jobs on\n  different threads), green after.\n- a_burst_longer_than_the_delay_waits_for_its_last_call: passes on both\n  old and new code (characterises item 2); mutation check -- counting the\n  deadline from the first call makes it fail.\n- Ran the window tests 3x, stable.\n\n## AGENTS.md\n- Added a section to src-tauri/AGENTS.md on the one-worker pattern.\nEOF\ncd src-tauri && cargo test 2>&1 | grep -E \"test result|FAILED|panicked\" ; cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings 2>&1 | tail -3","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":302,"cache_read_input_tokens":72057,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":302},"output_tokens":83,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1474f98a-9dc0-43f2-bfa3-a27872327722","uuid":"de358570-ec77-43dd-9558-804c4698cfe4","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:17:33.891Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8pYB6BD18cn5PgEWKXA","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01G9VTS62rJQTmNVLb1ozwat":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/webtorrent-desktop.memory-leaks-12-window-bounds-debounce-one-thread && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src-tauri/AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nanchor='## Gates\\n'\nadd='''## Background work from a window event gets one worker, not a thread each\n\nTauri delivers `WindowEvent`s on the UI thread, and a drag delivers\nhundreds of them. `window::Debounce` is the pattern for work that must\nleave that thread: one worker, started on the first call, sleeping on a\n`Condvar` until a deadline every call pushes forward, and ending when\nthe last clone is dropped. A `std::thread::spawn` per event is what it\nreplaced. Its tests make \"one worker\" observable by recording\n`std::thread::current().id()` from each job across several bursts.\n\n'''\ns=s.replace(anchor, add+anchor,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat >> .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Implemented\n- src-tauri/src/window.rs: `Debounce` now holds an `Arc<Handle>` over a\n  `Mutex<Pending>` + `Condvar`. `call` stores the newest job, moves the\n  deadline to now + delay, and lazily spawns the single worker. The worker\n  waits until the deadline passes unmoved, runs the job outside the lock\n  (wrapped in catch_unwind so a panicking job cannot kill the worker), and\n  exits once every clone is dropped and nothing is pending.\n- Public API unchanged (`new`, `call`, Clone, Debug); main.rs untouched.\n\n## Tests (src-tauri/src/window.rs)\n- every_burst_runs_on_the_one_worker: red on the old code (jobs on\n  different threads), green after.\n- a_burst_longer_than_the_delay_waits_for_its_last_call: passes on both\n  old and new code (characterises item 2); mutation check -- counting the\n  deadline from the first call makes it fail.\n- Ran the window tests 3x, stable.\n\n## AGENTS.md\n- Added a section to src-tauri/AGENTS.md on the one-worker pattern.\nEOF\ncd src-tauri && cargo test 2>&1 | grep -E \"test result|FAILED|panicked\" ; cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings 2>&1 | tail -3","timeout":600000}}}
