{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8pb4Qg5anr1p6LUgtFW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The window-bounds `Debounce` now uses a single worker thread instead of starting a new thread for every move or resize event. Its signature didn't change, so `main.rs` is untouched. All gates pass: `cargo test` (211 tests), `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy -- -D warnings`, and `npm test` (4224 tests).\n\n**How it works** (`src-tauri/src/window.rs`):\n1. Each `call` stores the newest job and moves the deadline to now plus the delay.\n2. The worker starts on the first call and waits until the deadline passes with no new call. It then runs the job outside the lock, so a call that arrives during the job isn't blocked.\n3. The worker exits once every copy of the `Debounce` is dropped and nothing is pending.\n\nI also added one thing the ticket didn't ask for: a job that panics is caught so it can't kill the worker. Before, a panic only took down that event's own thread; without the catch it would silently stop all later bounds saves.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `every_burst_runs_on_the_one_worker` checks the \"one worker\" claim by recording which thread runs each job across three bursts. It failed on the old code and passes now.\n- `a_burst_longer_than_the_delay_waits_for_its_last_call` covers the second checklist item. The old code already behaved this way, so this test was never red. To show it isn't a test that can't fail, I temporarily changed the code to count the deadline from the first call instead of the last, and it failed.\n- The two existing debounce tests are unchanged. The window tests passed three runs in a row.\n\nTo run `cargo test` in this worktree I first had to run `npm run build:tauri`. I added a short section to `src-tauri/AGENTS.md` describing the one-worker pattern for work triggered by window events.\n\nThere are three commits. `.nightralph/notes.md` is left uncommitted as instructed.\n\n[x] After a burst of calls, the job runs exactly once\n[x] The job does not run before the delay has passed since the last call"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":293,"cache_read_input_tokens":74029,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":293},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1474f98a-9dc0-43f2-bfa3-a27872327722","uuid":"36283355-d998-4695-a6e3-9cddc5ec4214","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:18:11.883Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8pb484aYiC8LR6TgSwC"}
